                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On November 19, 1951, Secretary of State Acheson spoke before the First Committee
                    of the General Assembly in support and elaboration of the tripartite resolution
                    on regulation, limitation, and balanced reduction of all armed forces and all
                    armaments, document A/C.1/667 <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>. For the
                    summary record of his remarks, see United Nations, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Official Records of the General Assembly, Sixth Session, First
                        Committee</hi>, pages 7–10 (hereafter cited as GA (VI), <hi rendition="#italic">First Committee</hi>). For the
                    full text of the address, Department of State press release 1040, November 20,
                    1951, see <hi rendition="#italic">Documents on Disarmament, 1945–1959</hi>,
                    volume I, pages 309–330.</p>
            </div>
